module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.AbelianAmalgam.LineNormalizers.Descent.QuotientIdentification.Original
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.AbelianAmalgam.LineNormalizers.Descent.QuotientIdentification.ResidualFactors
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.AbelianAmalgam.LineNormalizers.Descent.QuotientIdentification.ThompsonLift

/-!
# Original line-normalizer quotient identification

The original centralizer factor is recognized by its three-coset action,
using the actual maximum-elementary Thompson subgroup to exclude a normal
Sylow subgroup. The resulting `G_E/O₂(G_E) ≃ S₃ × S₃` preserves the initial
marked `⟨Y_E,τ⟩` factor and the original centralizer image. Intrinsic core,
coordinate-kernel and residual-intersection comparisons are included.

The residual images are the two marked alternating factors, giving actual
equivalences `X_E/O₂(X_E) ≃ C₃` and `Y_E/O₂(Y_E) ≃ C₃` compatible with
the same product map. Supplying the proved second-factor image to the
Thompson lifting argument gives `X_E = [X_E, J(R)]`, with no remaining
image or action premise. The nontrivial Thompson action comes from the
original maximum-elementary family and the index of the original `I₀`.

The conditional input `Inputs` retains the preceding geometric, Sylow and
recognition data and the explicitly supplied descent identity
`M_E = Y_E T_E`. Constructing these inputs, and assembling the other clauses
of full Lemma 15.3.67, remains with the parent descent development.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), proof of
Lemma 15.3.67, printed pp.1153–1154, PDF pp.1170–1171.
-/

public section

open Subgroup Stellmacher

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.AbelianAmalgam.Descent.QuotientIdentification

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G]
variable {M Y T V E : Subgroup G} [IsMulCommutative V]

/-- The original residual is generated by its commutators with the actual
elementary Thompson subgroup of `R = C_T(V)`. The second-factor image needed
for the lift is the proved image of the original `X_E`. -/
theorem lineX_eq_commutator_thompson (s : Inputs M Y T V E) :
    lineX E = ⁅lineX E, elementaryAbelianMaxJ (T ⊓ centralizer (V : Set G))⁆ :=
  ThompsonLift.lineX_eq_commutator_thompson_of_image s (originalProductMap_lineX s)

/-- The same equality with `J(T_E)`, as used immediately after 15.3.67. -/
theorem lineX_eq_commutator_sylowThompson (s : Inputs M Y T V E) :
    lineX E = ⁅lineX E, elementaryAbelianMaxJ (lineT T E)⁆ := by
  rw [s.thompson_eq]
  exact lineX_eq_commutator_thompson s

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.AbelianAmalgam.Descent.QuotientIdentification
